cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "dualmesh: coupled heat transfer, solid mechanics and incompressible flow by the finite element method and the dual mesh control domain method"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: 0.2.0
license: LGPL-2.1-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/MohamedAbdulHameed/dualmesh"
url: "https://github.com/MohamedAbdulHameed/dualmesh"
abstract: >-
  dualmesh solves coupled problems of heat transfer, solid
  mechanics and incompressible flow, and partial differential equations
  written as text. It discretizes a problem by the finite element method
  (FEM), and a problem with an equal-order flow by the dual mesh control
  domain method (DMCDM), which conserves the transported quantity in every
  control domain. Coupled problems are solved together by Newton's method,
  with exact Jacobians from automatic differentiation. The core is written
  in C++20 with PETSc and MPI, and it is driven from Python or from YAML case
  files.
keywords:
  - dual mesh control domain method
  - finite element method
  - fluid dynamics
  - solid mechanics
  - heat transfer
  - partial differential equations
  - multiphysics
authors:
